Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P9.7 slice 2: the port Options screen in battle (hold the main loop)

P9.7, slice 2 (battle). The battle has no menu the port controls, so the
entry is a button: while the battle's command menu waits for the player
(FIGHTSTG_updateCommandMenu, TASK_RUN) Select (Minus on the Switch) with no
shoulder button held calls dw3_port_battle_options_poll, which opens the port
Options screen (the in-game mode of slice 1, drawn by the native overlay) and
asks the main loop to hold the battle.

The hold is in main(): while dw3_port_battle_options_hold_frame() is 1 the
iteration does not run the task list, the widescreen frame or drawFrame, so no
task, timer, event, gauge, animation or random countdown moves, no task reads
the pad, and nothing is submitted (the display keeps the last picture). It
only presents (VSync), updates the pad and runs the port's polls, the file
cache and the sound loader; the music keeps playing because the sequencer ticks
in the vsync callback. RANDOM.next() is skipped so the roll sequence is the one
the battle would have had. When the screen closes, the port gives the game's
vsync clocks (GFX.timeCounter, frameTimeCounter, GAME.playTime.frames) back as
they were: the callback kept adding to them, and the battle compares absolute
GFX times (messages, arrows) and takes its frame length from them. A restart
chord while held forgets the hold.

Without the native overlay the entry is not offered
(dw3_port_battle_options_enabled() is 0).

